    "result_text": "Done. **`BUILD SUCCESS`** \u2014 the full suite is green (1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe salutation feature follows the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (like `telephoneDisplay`, `membershipNumber`): a stored input field on `OwnerFields`, a read-only derived field on `Owner`, backed by a transient entity getter that MapStruct auto-maps.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from this at build time):\n   - Added `title` as an optional editable string to the `OwnerFields` schema (input).\n   - Added `salutation` as a `readOnly` derived string to the `Owner` schema (output).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `title` column field with getter/setter, plus a `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. Because the DTO property name matches the getter, MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper change needed) \u2014 the same way `getTitle()`/`setTitle()` auto-map the input field.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** for all four databases (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `title` column, since the test profile runs with `ddl-auto=none` and relies on the SQL schema.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`** \u2014 copies `title` alongside the other editable fields on update, for consistency.\n\nThe acceptance test posts `title: \"DR\"`, `lastName: \"who\"` and reads back `salutation: \"DR who\"` \u2014 which now passes.",
